# Git workflow

This repo’s default branch is `main` (treat `master` the same).

## Branch

- Never commit, amend, or push on `main` / `master`.
- If you are on `main` / `master` and files need to change, create a new branch first (`git checkout -b …`) so the working-tree changes come along. Then edit on that branch.
- Stay on the current feature branch if we are already off `main`.

## Commit and push — user must ask

- Never create a local commit unless the user explicitly asks to commit.
- Never push unless the user explicitly asks to push.
- “Commit and push” means both. “Commit” does not mean push. Making file changes does not mean commit.
- After editing, stop. The user verifies before commit almost every time. Do not assume the work is ready to go.
